---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Button from '../../components/Button.astro';

const SITE = 'https://warrenlabs.com';
const url = `${SITE}/learn`;
const description =
  'Evergreen guides to how headphones and the gear around them actually work: decisive, honest, no mysticism. Written by someone who spent a career measuring headphones.';

const published = [
  {
    href: '/learn/importing-your-own-measurement',
    section: 'Measurement & tuning',
    title: 'How to import your own headphone measurement',
    teaser:
      'Where to find a measurement file, which one to pick, and the raw-versus-compensated mistake that quietly ruins the result.',
  },
  {
    href: '/learn/how-to-read-a-frequency-response-graph',
    section: 'Measurement & tuning',
    title: 'How to read a frequency-response graph',
    teaser:
      'What the axes mean, how to read the peaks and dips against a target, and what a graph can and can’t tell you, without the mysticism.',
  },
  {
    href: '/learn/do-i-need-a-headphone-amp',
    section: 'Understanding the gear',
    title: 'Do you need a headphone amp?',
    teaser:
      'Usually not. Most headphones and nearly all IEMs run clean off a dongle. Here is how to tell when you actually need one.',
  },
  {
    href: '/learn/open-back-vs-closed-back-headphones',
    section: 'Understanding the gear',
    title: 'Open-back vs closed-back headphones',
    teaser:
      'One sounds more spacious; the other isolates and hits harder. Neither is “better”. How to choose by where and around whom you listen.',
  },
  {
    href: '/learn/what-headphone-impedance-means',
    section: 'Understanding the gear',
    title: 'What headphone impedance means (and when to care)',
    teaser:
      'Impedance and sensitivity together decide whether a headphone is “hard to drive”. How to read both, and when the specs don’t matter at all.',
  },
  {
    href: '/learn/target-curves-explained',
    section: 'Measurement & tuning',
    title: 'Target curves: Harman, diffuse-field, and a house curve',
    teaser:
      'Why flat doesn’t sound neutral, what each target actually represents, and why none of them is objectively “correct.”',
  },
  {
    href: '/learn/why-two-rigs-cant-share-an-axis',
    section: 'Measurement & tuning',
    title: 'Why you can’t compare measurements from two different rigs',
    teaser:
      'A curve describes the headphone and the bench it was measured on. Where rigs disagree, why compensation hides it, and the one rule we hold ourselves to.',
  },
  {
    href: '/learn/what-a-dac-is',
    section: 'Understanding the gear',
    title: 'What a DAC is (and when you actually need one)',
    teaser:
      'You already own a DAC. When an external one actually helps, and why it’s not the fidelity upgrade it’s sold as.',
  },
  {
    href: '/learn/wireless-and-bluetooth-headphones',
    section: 'Understanding the gear',
    title: 'Wireless & Bluetooth: what you actually give up',
    teaser:
      'Latency, battery, and control over the DAC, not, usually, obvious sound quality. Why the codec wars are mostly noise.',
  },
  {
    href: '/learn/what-cables-can-and-cant-do',
    section: 'Understanding the gear',
    title: 'What cables can (and can’t) do',
    teaser:
      'Build, length, connectors, and microphonics are real; “warmth” and “blacker backgrounds” from a pricey cable are not. The honest line.',
  },
  {
    href: '/learn/iems-vs-over-ear-headphones',
    section: 'Understanding the gear',
    title: 'IEMs vs over-ear headphones',
    teaser:
      'In-ears seal and isolate; over-ears are roomier and comfier for long sessions. How to choose by isolation, comfort, and fit.',
  },
  {
    href: '/learn/why-level-matching-changes-everything',
    section: 'Measurement & tuning',
    title: 'Why level-matching changes everything',
    teaser:
      'Louder always sounds “better,” so unmatched comparisons are rigged. The single most important, and most skipped, discipline in audio.',
  },
  {
    href: '/learn/what-eq-can-and-cant-do',
    section: 'Measurement & tuning',
    title: 'What EQ can and can’t do',
    teaser:
      'The biggest cheap upgrade you’re not using, and why it doesn’t “ruin” sound. What it changes (tone) and what it can’t (physics).',
  },
  {
    href: '/learn/how-to-listen-for-tonal-balance',
    section: 'Listening',
    title: 'How to listen for tonal balance',
    teaser:
      'You don’t need golden ears. You need a method: familiar tracks, matched levels, and listening by region instead of for “detail.”',
  },
  {
    href: '/learn/choosing-your-first-serious-headphone',
    section: 'Listening',
    title: 'Choosing your first serious headphone',
    teaser:
      'Decide three things: where you listen, what drives it, and the sound you like, and the field narrows itself. A framework, not a ranked list.',
  },
  {
    href: '/learn/headphone-driver-types',
    section: 'Understanding the gear',
    title: 'Driver types: dynamic, planar, and electrostatic',
    teaser:
      'What each driver technology actually changes about the sound, and why the tuning still matters more than the label.',
  },
  {
    href: '/learn/does-headphone-burn-in-do-anything',
    section: 'Measurement & tuning',
    title: 'Does headphone burn-in do anything?',
    teaser:
      'Mostly a myth for modern headphones. The measurements barely budge. What you hear is your ears adapting. The evidence-based take.',
  },
  {
    href: '/learn/buying-used-headphones',
    section: 'Listening',
    title: 'Buying used headphones without getting burned',
    teaser:
      'Where the value and the discontinued classics live, with a five-minute channel/pad/cable check so a deal doesn’t become a repair.',
  },
];

const upcoming = [];

const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: `${SITE}/` },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Learn', item: url },
    ],
  },
];

const SECTIONS = ['Understanding the gear', 'Measurement & tuning', 'Listening'];
const grouped = SECTIONS.map((section) => ({
  section,
  items: published.filter((a) => a.section === section),
})).filter((g) => g.items.length);
---

<Layout title="Learn · Warren Labs" description={description} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <Nav variant="home" />

  <section class="wrap learn">
    <nav class="crumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><span aria-current="page">Learn</span>
    </nav>

    <span class="eyebrow">Learn</span>
    <h1>Learn headphones, honestly.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Evergreen guides to how this gear actually works: decisive, honest, and free of mysticism. No
      &ldquo;liquid mids,&rdquo; no format wars. Just clear answers from someone who spent a career measuring
      headphones and building the tools to compare them.
    </p>

    {
      grouped.map((g) => (
        <section class="pub-group">
          <h2 class="group-h">{g.section}</h2>
          <div class="pubs">
            {g.items.map((a) => (
              <a class="pub" href={a.href}>
                <h3>{a.title}</h3>
                <p>{a.teaser}</p>
                <span class="pub-go">Read it &rarr;</span>
              </a>
            ))}
          </div>
        </section>
      ))
    }

    {
      upcoming.length > 0 && (
        <div class="soon">
          <div class="soon-head">
            <h2>In the works</h2>
            <p>The core library above covers the essentials. These get written when there’s something worth adding:</p>
          </div>
          {upcoming.map((g) => (
            <div class="soon-group">
              <div class="soon-sec">{g.section}</div>
              <ul>
                {g.items.map((it) => (
                  <li>{it}</li>
                ))}
              </ul>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      )
    }

    <div class="learn-cta">
      <div>
        <h2>Want to hear the difference, not just read about it?</h2>
        <p>Attune turns a measurement into something you can actually listen to. Free, no subscription.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="learn-cta-btns">
        <Button href="/attune" variant="primary">Get Attune, free</Button>
        <Button href="/attune" variant="ghost" data-signup data-intent="notify">Get the occasional update</Button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer variant="home" />
</Layout>

<style>
  .learn {
    padding: 56px 24px 24px;
  }
  .crumb {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 11.5px;
    color: var(--muted-2);
    display: flex;
    gap: 9px;
    margin-bottom: 26px;
  }
  .crumb a:hover {
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .crumb [aria-current] {
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .learn h1 {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(36px, 6vw, 58px);
    line-height: 1.03;
    margin: 12px 0 0;
  }
  .lede {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    max-width: 60ch;
    margin: 20px 0 0;
  }
  .pubs {
    display: grid;
    gap: 16px;
    margin-top: 18px;
  }
  .pub-group {
    margin-top: 44px;
  }
  .group-h {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 24px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin: 0;
    padding-bottom: 6px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-soft);
  }
  .pub {
    display: block;
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 26px 28px;
    transition:
      border-color 0.2s,
      transform 0.2s;
  }
  .pub:hover {
    border-color: var(--accent-line);
    transform: translateY(-2px);
  }
  .pub-sec {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent-soft);
  }
  .pub h3 {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 26px;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .pub p {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 15.5px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 10px 0 0;
    max-width: 62ch;
  }
  .pub-go {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: 16px;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .pub:hover .pub-go {
    color: var(--accent-soft);
  }
  .soon {
    margin-top: 56px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding-top: 34px;
  }
  .soon-head h2 {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 27px;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .soon-head p {
    color: var(--muted-2);
    font-size: 14px;
    margin: 8px 0 0;
  }
  .soon-group {
    margin-top: 26px;
  }
  .soon-sec {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }
  .soon-group ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 1px;
  }
  .soon-group li {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 15.5px;
    padding: 11px 0 11px 22px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line-soft);
    position: relative;
  }
  .soon-group li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 3px;
    top: 18px;
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    border: 1px solid var(--muted-2);
    border-radius: 50%;
  }
  .learn-cta {
    margin-top: 56px;
    background: linear-gradient(120deg, rgba(255, 158, 44, 0.07), var(--surface) 55%);
    border: 1px solid var(--accent-line);
    border-radius: 18px;
    padding: 30px 32px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 24px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .learn-cta h2 {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 24px;
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 22ch;
  }
  .learn-cta p {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 15px;
    margin: 8px 0 0;
    max-width: 46ch;
  }
  .learn-cta-btns {
    display: flex;
    gap: 12px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
</style>
